    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0118" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1946v05/pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/12–746: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in India</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Merrell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-12-07T13:00:00-05:00">December 7, 1946—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>912. Brit Govt has told us through Brit Emb here it believes it might be helpful
                    if we expressed informally to Congress leaders, particularly Nehru, views this
                    Govt as indicated last two paragraphs <pb facs="0119" n="101" xml:id="pg101"/>
                    Deptel 893 Nov 30 to you.<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d62-f1"/> Upon arrival Nehru New Delhi and prior meeting Congress
                    Working Committee tomorrow night, please emphasize to him views this Govt as
                    expressed aforementioned telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d62-f1" n="55" xml:id="d62-f1-content">
                <p>Same as telegram 7979 to London, <ref target="#pg97">p. 97</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
